{% comment %}
  ==================================================================
  GS PRODUCT BADGE
  ==================================================================
  USAGE: render 'gs-product-badge', cardProduct: product

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  DEFAULTS NOW MATCH WHAT v3 ACTUALLY HAS CONFIGURED
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Every badge is gated on a gs-shopify-v3 THEME SETTING with no entry in
  Dawn's config/settings_schema.json, so all of them are nil here. The
  rule adopted across this port is that a missing setting means ENABLED,
  so an absent schema entry fails open rather than silently hiding a
  feature.

  For badges that rule was WRONG, and reading v3's settings_data.json
  showed exactly how wrong. Production has:

      new_label       true      -> fail open is correct
      sale_label      FALSE     -> fail open showed a badge v3 hides
      preorder_label  FALSE     -> fail open showed a badge v3 hides
      soldout_label   false     -> already opt-in

  So the Dawn theme was putting SALE and PRE-ORDER badges on products
  that carry neither on the live site. Both are opt-IN now, matching
  production. New stays fail-open, which matches too.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  SOLD OUT IS OPT-IN FOR A DIFFERENT REASON
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  v3 rendered it with NO availability check at all, so defaulting it on
  would badge every in-stock product.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  CUSTOM TAG BADGES - INDEX MISMATCH, DOCUMENTED NOT FIXED
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  v3 names these `custom_tag` and `custom_tag_label` for the FIRST pair,
  then custom_tag_1..9. This loop reads custom_tag_0..9, so the first
  pair would never match. Left as is because none of these settings
  exist in Dawn's schema yet - fix the loop when they are added.

  For reference, v3 has these configured:
    USA 250, Limited Edition, Club Exclusive, ClubEA (Club Early
    Access), new, Ready To Ship (Ships Now), Best Seller, Mainline Sale
    (Sale)

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  EARLIER FIXES
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  - FILTER INSIDE AN IF CONDITION: `if product_tag | downcase == tag`
    raised "Expected end_of_string but found pipe" and broke EVERY
    product card. Precomputed now.
  - v3's sold-out badge had no availability check.
  - v3's "new" badge iterated every collection AND every product inside
    each, per card, and Liquid caps collection.products at 50 - so
    products past the 50th silently never got it. Reads
    cardProduct.collections instead.
  - Sale badge compared compare_at_price_MAX against price_MIN, so one
    discounted variant marked the whole product on sale.
  - Carries its own stylesheet; these rules lived in gs-card-product.css,
    which only loads when a CARD renders.
  ==================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  unless cardProduct
    break
  endunless

  # NEW fails open - v3 has this on.
  assign allow_new = true
  if settings.new_label == false
    assign allow_new = false
  endif

  # SALE and PRE-ORDER are opt-IN - v3 has both OFF. See the header note.
  assign allow_sale = false
  if settings.sale_label == true
    assign allow_sale = true
  endif

  assign allow_preorder = false
  if settings.preorder_label == true
    assign allow_preorder = true
  endif

  assign badge_count = 0
  assign is_new = false
  assign first_variant = cardProduct.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}

{{ 'gs-product-badge.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%} NEW {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if allow_new and cardProduct.available -%}
  {%- liquid
    if settings.new_collection_label
      for tagged_collection in settings.add_new_collection
        for product_collection in cardProduct.collections
          if product_collection.handle == tagged_collection.handle
            assign is_new = true
            break
          endif
        endfor
        if is_new
          break
        endif
      endfor
    else
      assign days = settings.days_ago_created | default: 40
      assign now_days = 'now' | date: '%s' | divided_by: 86400
      assign published_days = cardProduct.published_at | date: '%s' | divided_by: 86400
      assign day_difference = now_days | minus: published_days
      if day_difference <= days
        assign is_new = true
      endif
    endif
  -%}

  {%- if is_new -%}
    <span class="product-badge new">{{ 'products.product.badges.new' | t }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} SALE {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if allow_sale and cardProduct.compare_at_price_min > cardProduct.price_min -%}
  {%- if settings.sale_label_with_percentage -%}
    <span class="product-badge sale-percentage">
      {{ 'products.product.badges.sale' | t }}
      <span class="sale-percentage-off">
        {{- cardProduct.compare_at_price_min
          | minus: cardProduct.price_min
          | times: 100
          | divided_by: cardProduct.compare_at_price_min -}}%
      </span>
    </span>
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="product-badge sale">{{ 'products.product.badges.sale' | t }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} PREORDER {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if allow_preorder and first_variant -%}
  {%- if first_variant.inventory_quantity <= 0 and first_variant.inventory_policy == 'continue' -%}
    <span class="product-badge preorder-badge">{{ 'products.product.badges.preorder' | t }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} CUSTOM tag badges - max 2. See the index note in the header. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- for i in (0..9) -%}
  {%- if badge_count >= 2 -%}
    {%- break -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign label_key = 'custom_tag_label_' | append: i
    assign tag_key = 'custom_tag_' | append: i
    assign label = settings[label_key]
    assign matched = false
  -%}

  {%- if label != blank -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign custom_tags = settings[tag_key] | downcase | split: ','
      for tag in custom_tags
        assign clean_tag = tag | strip
        for product_tag in cardProduct.tags
          # Precomputed - a filter cannot appear inside an if condition.
          assign product_tag_down = product_tag | downcase
          if product_tag_down == clean_tag
            assign matched = true
            break
          endif
        endfor
        if matched
          break
        endif
      endfor
    -%}

    {%- if matched -%}
      <span class="product-badge custom-badge">{{ label }}</span>
      {%- assign badge_count = badge_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%}
  SOLD OUT stays opt-IN. v3 rendered it with no availability check, so
  defaulting this on would badge every in-stock product.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.soldout_label == true and cardProduct.available == false -%}
  <span class="product-badge sold-badge">{{ 'products.product.badges.soldout' | t }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
